module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_step_binds_env_from_a_step_output_its_condition_can_skip

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_step_binds_env_from_a_step_output_its_condition_can_skip: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_step_binds_env_from_a_step_output_its_condition_can_skip" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "a step's env binds ${{ steps.<id>.outputs.<name> }} where the producing step carries a condition the CONSUMER's position does not imply: when that condition is false the producer is skipped, the expression resolves to the EMPTY STRING (GitHub Actions does not fail the binding), and the consumer runs with a silently-empty credential. Detection lives only inside the consumer, so the failure surfaces as the consumer's own typed refusal -- correct fail-closed behaviour, but the workflow itself stays green up to that point, and a consumer that does NOT refuse turns the empty string into a wrong-behaving run. The defect is a missing proof: the emit never checked that the producer's condition is implied-live at the consumer's position.",

    "SIGHTING, gunb-ai/gunbc fleet-converge run 43923411255 (2026-11-16, the first NO-OP gcp_iam_converge): the srv15 versions-metadata read step bound WIF_ACCESS_TOKEN to the post-wait re-mint (steps.wif_auth_iam_observe.outputs.access_token) whose own condition is steps.gcp_iam_request.outputs.approved == 'true'. A no-op converge files no request, so there is no approval, the re-mint is skipped, the binding resolves empty, and the read refused typed -- 'srv15-bmc-versions: Srv15SecretReadCredentialRefused; the job could not present a workload identity' (exit 1). The approved path had always masked it (run 43880588775 had diffs -> approval -> the re-mint minted). The manager ruled against a '|| fallback' patch -- 'whichever token happens to exist' is authority chosen by step history, the very class this row files -- and for the read's credential to be its OWN declared dependency: a dedicated iam-observe mint under the read's own condition, its sole consumer the read (fleet_converge_srv15_read_wif_auth_step). test.claim.workflow_dispatch_input_witness pins the mint's service account, provider, condition-equality with the read, and sole consumption.",

    "RUNG: mitigatable -- the fleet_converge emit's step claims pin each credential binding to a producer verified present-at-consumer-position FOR THE STEPS THE WITNESS ROSTERS; an unrostered binding still passes. ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: the emit resolves every ${{ steps.<id>.outputs }} reference to its producer and refuses where the producer's condition is not implied-live at the consumer's position (the consumer's own condition, or its enclosing job's, entails the producer's) -- so a credential whose existence depends on which steps happened to run cannot be written down.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
